# MANIFEST.sha256 - evidence tree for the v30a availability declaration
# Generated: 2026-08-20 23:53:18 UTC
#
# SCOPE. One line per committed file, in `sha256  path` form (two spaces, lowercase
# hex, forward slashes). Paths are relative to the directory holding this manifest
# (the `evidence/` directory of the repository), so `sha256sum -c MANIFEST.sha256`
# run from inside `evidence/` verifies the tree as-is. The `../` lines are the
# repository-root files the ceremony commits alongside this tree: the declaration,
# `PRIOR_ART_VERIFICATION.md`, `PRACTICES.md` and `prereg-signing-key.asc` (the
# ASCII-armored public key, added R69/B2.3). ALL of them must verify. Do not restate
# their COUNT here - it read "three" while there were four; derive it:
#     grep -cE '^[0-9a-f]{64}  \.\./' MANIFEST.sha256
#
# PATH RESOLUTION FOR THE DECLARATION. Relative evidence paths quoted inside
# AVAILABILITY_DECLARATION.md (e.g. `t4\fixture_manifest_35col_DRAFT.json`,
# `f5\DEVIATIONS_entry_SKELETON.md`) resolve relative to `evidence\fixture_spike\`.
# Those paths were written against the scratchpad build directory named in the
# declaration preamble; that directory is transient, `evidence\fixture_spike\` is
# its committed replacement, and the two are byte-identical for every file listed
# below, with the two `f4` exceptions R14 creates (next paragraph). Archive paths
# quoted in the declaration remain under `C:\Users\ttbea\OneDrive\Desktop\MBO_2025`
# (read-only) and are NOT reproduced here.
#
# R14 - SINGLE NORMATIVE COPY OF THE DECLARATION. The repository-root
# AVAILABILITY_DECLARATION.md is the ONE normative copy; the evidence tree carries a
# pointer plus a recorded hash, never a duplicate. `fixture_spike/f4/` accordingly
# holds `DECLARATION_POINTER.md` and nothing else. Two consequences for this
# manifest. (1) `f4/availability_declaration_DRAFT.md`, previously listed here as a
# byte-duplicate of the declaration, has been DELETED from the tree. Under R18 it has
# also been RETIRED at source, to
# `fixture_spike\_retired\availability_declaration_DRAFT.RETIRED-2026-08-13.md`, and is
# INERT: no build copy of the declaration exists, the repository-root file is edited in
# place, and nothing is copied over it. The `../AVAILABILITY_DECLARATION.md` line below
# is the sole hash of those bytes. (2) `f4/DECLARATION_POINTER.md` is the one
# file in this manifest with no counterpart in the build directory - it is written
# for the committed tree. Every other listed file remains byte-identical to its
# build-directory original. The pointer's recorded hash and the
# `../AVAILABILITY_DECLARATION.md` line are rewritten in the same pass, always; a
# hash carried forward from an earlier sync is prohibited (R15).
#
# `fixture_spike/_snapshots/availability_declaration_PRE_R9.md` is NOT a second copy
# under R14: it is a frozen historical snapshot, named for the state it froze, not
# maintained, and never a candidate for "the current declaration".
#
# SIBLING BUILD DIRECTORIES. `author_review/`, `ceremony/` and `errata/` sit beside
# `fixture_spike/` here because they sit beside it in the transient build directory
# too - they are build records of the read-through, ceremony-preparation and errata
# work, not of the fixture spike. Relative paths quoted between them (e.g.
# `errata\HISTORY_lesson_line_STAGED.md` in `ceremony/COMMIT_PLAN.md`) therefore
# resolve relative to `evidence\`, not to `evidence\fixture_spike\`. They carry no
# normative content; `AVAILABILITY_DECLARATION.md` and `PREREG.md` remain the only
# sources of measurement semantics.
#
# `../PRIOR_ART_VERIFICATION.md`. The second `../` line. This file is a repository-root
# registration artifact, not part of the evidence tree, and it is listed for the same
# reason the declaration is: the ceremony commits it, and two documents the tag hashes
# (`HISTORY.md` H-34 and `DESIGN.md` §2.11) cite it by name - H-34 by sha256 as well.
# Until this pass no manifest line covered it, so `sha256sum -c` could not tell whether
# the file those documents cite was the file present. It can now. Whether the file also
# takes a seventh tag-time hash is an open author decision recorded in
# `ceremony/COMMIT_PLAN.md` §3.3; this line settles the manifest question only, and
# takes no position on that one.
#
# `../PRACTICES.md`. The third `../` line, added when the file landed at the repository
# root. It is a repository-root artifact and is explicitly NON-NORMATIVE - it binds
# nothing, no gate verdict depends on it, and it is not part of the registration. It is
# listed for coverage, not for authority: the ceremony commits it, the declaration points
# into it where the v30a scrub moved a practice out, and a reader following such a pointer
# should be able to tell whether the file present is the file the pointer was written
# against. It takes no tag-time hash; the six-file tag hash set is unchanged by its
# presence.
#
# EXCLUSIONS. Two rules were applied when relocating: no single file larger than
# 20 MiB (20971520 bytes), and no `.pkl` file at any size. Every excluded file is
# accounted for by path, sha256, size and a reproduction note in the
# EXCLUDED-HASH-ONLY section at the tail of this manifest. Nothing was deleted from
# the build directory; exclusion here means "not copied into the repository".
#
# COUNTS. committed files: 240 under fixture_spike/ + 8 under the sibling build
#         directories + 3 repository-root files = 251.
#         committed bytes: 13309008 (12655650 fixture_spike/ +
#         342928 siblings + 310430 repository-root).
#         excluded files: 14; excluded bytes: 1542317685.
#
# This manifest does not list itself.
#
